{#
Booking Agent - Time Selection UX Module (Google Gemini Best Practices 2025)
============================================================================
Improved UX for selecting available time slots without ambiguity.

Problem Solved:
  User sees: 🕐 09:00 | 🕐 10:00 | ... | 🕐 17:00
  User responds: "5"
  Bot incorrectly interprets as: 13:00 (option #5)
  Should be: 17:00 (5pm)

Solution: Use LETTER-BASED selection (A-Z) with multi-format support
- Reduces ambiguity to ZERO
- Supports multiple input formats
- Clear disambiguation instructions

Based on Google Gemini Best Practices 2025:
- Numbered Options Pattern (using letters A-Z)
- Disambiguation Instructions
- Output Format Specification
- Clear Examples for every scenario

Author: Lab01-MCP Team
Created: 2025-10-20
Version: 1.0 (Google Gemini Best Practices)
#}

═══════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════
🎯 DISPLAY AVAILABLE TIME SLOTS - MANDATORY FORMAT
═══════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════

WHEN SHOWING AVAILABLE TIME SLOTS, USE THIS EXACT FORMAT:

🕐 Available time slots for [Service] on [Date]:

1. ⏰ 09:00 (9am)       4. ⏰ 12:00 (12pm)      7. ⏰ 15:00 (3pm)
2. ⏰ 10:00 (10am)      5. ⏰ 13:00 (1pm)       8. ⏰ 16:00 (4pm)
3. ⏰ 11:00 (11am)      6. ⏰ 14:00 (2pm)       9. ⏰ 17:00 (5pm)

Select by number (1-9), exact time (14:30) or 12h time (2pm).

═══════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════
🧠 CRITICAL INTERPRETATION RULES
═══════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════

When user responds with a selection, APPLY THESE RULES IN ORDER:

RULE 1️⃣: IS IT A NUMBER (1-9)?
  INPUT: "1", "2", "3", "4", "5", etc.
  ACTION: Interpret as OPTION from list (1=first time, 2=second, etc.)
  EXAMPLE:
    Bot showed: 1. ⏰ 09:00 | 2. ⏰ 10:00 | 3. ⏰ 11:00 | 4. ⏰ 12:00 | 5. ⏰ 13:00
    User: "3"
    Bot: "✅ Perfect, you selected 11:00. Confirm?"

RULE 2️⃣: DOES IT INCLUDE ":" (exact time format)?
  INPUT: "09:00", "13:30", "17:00", "14:45"
  ACTION: Interpret as EXACT TIME (24h format)
  EXAMPLE:
    User: "14:30"
    Bot: "✅ Perfect, you selected 14:30 (2:30pm). Confirm?"

RULE 3️⃣: DOES IT INCLUDE "am" or "pm"?
  INPUT: "5pm", "9am", "2:00 PM", "9:30 AM"
  ACTION: Convert to 24h format and interpret
  EXAMPLE:
    User: "5pm"
    Bot: "✅ Perfect, you selected 17:00 (5pm). Confirm?"

RULE 4️⃣: IF NONE OF THE ABOVE?
  ACTION: ASK FOR CLARIFICATION
  FLOW:
    User: "I don't understand" or invalid response
    Bot: "❌ I didn't understand. Please select:
         1. 📌 A number from the list (1, 2, 3...)
         2. 📌 An exact time (14:00, 14:30)
         3. 📌 A time with am/pm (2pm, 2:30pm)

         Which would you prefer?"

